---
description: Keep current language in a locked LanguageStore and notify LocaleNotifier on every change, including loadFromSettings
globs: i18n/**/*.{h,cpp}
alwaysApply: false
---

# Language store, not a bare global

Do not keep the current UI language in a file-scope `g_language`. Put it in a `LanguageStore` (mutex next to the enum, Meyers singleton). Snapshot under the lock, persist `QSettings` under the same lock, emit `LocaleNotifier` **outside** it.

Every mutation that changes the language must notify — `setLanguage` **and** `loadFromSettings`. A silent load after widgets subscribe leaves stale copy.

```cpp
// BAD — global; load does not notify
Language g_language = Language::English;
void loadFromSettings() { g_language = readSettings(); }

// GOOD — locked store; notify only after the lock is released
void setLanguage(Language language) {
  notifyLanguageChangedIf(LanguageStore::instance().setLanguageAndPersist(language));
}
void loadFromSettings() {
  notifyLanguageChangedIf(LanguageStore::instance().loadFromSettings());
}
```

Do not lazy-load `QSettings` from `currentLanguage()`: org/app name is set after `QApplication` exists. Call `loadFromSettings()` from `main` after that, before creating windows.
